VISUAL: Hugging Face page for MiniMax Music 3, showing model details and architecture.
AUDIO: 'All right, YouTube. What is good? It\'s your boy Rebel back with another video. And today, we are taking a look at Minimax Music 3. So, Minimax Music 3 is a high-performance music generation model for creating complete songs up to'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '5 minutes long. Conditioned on lyrics and a detailed music description, it generates structurally coherent songs with expressive vocals, evolving arrangements, and stable long-form audio quality. Minimax Music 3 combines an 8'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'billion global LLM for long-range musical structure and a 0.6 billion local LLM for frame-level acoustic detail and a continuous hidden state'

[00:37] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Hugging Face page for MiniMax Music 3, showing details on fine-grained music control.
AUDIO: 'synthesis system based on flow matching and flow VAE. The model produces 32 kHz 16-bit stereo wave audio. The model natively supports full song generation'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'up to 5 minutes and maintains musical themes, rhythm, vocal identity, arrangement progression across long sequences, enabling complete structures such as intro, verse, pre-chorus, chorus, bridge,'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'instrumental breaks, and outros. And the model has very fine-grain music control, accepting two complementary inputs, which are lyrics and description. So, you are going to be putting in your'

[01:15] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Hugging Face page for MiniMax Music 3, showing details on structured captions for control.
AUDIO: 'lyrics with these explicit section tags. And the musical description will define the musical style, emotional progression, vocal performance, instrumentation, arrangement, and production profile. The vocal details'

[01:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'include vocal gender. And for more precise control, they recommend using structured captions with three sections for global metadata, vocal details, and arrangement. So, for the global metadata, you\'re going to want to'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'include the genre, the subgenre, the beats per minute, the key, the scale, emotional progression, listening scenario, and production profile. The vocal details will include your vocal gender, your timbre, the performance'

[01:54] [scene:intro]
VISUAL: Hugging Face page for MiniMax Music 3, showing details on structured captions for control.
AUDIO: 'style, any harmonies you want to include, any backing vocals and vocal effects, and the arrangement needs to be assessed. So, you need to provide primary and secondary instruments such as guitar, lead guitar, and then section'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'level instrument evolution. So, you know, crescendos from the strings or, you know, build up from the drums. You know, those that would be a good example for the section level. You need to'

